HID: magicmouse: options for Tactile on top of the one-click-per-press fix

Applies after 0001. Not meant for upstream as it is: these are the knobs the
Tactile settings app turns.

- haptic_finger_extra, haptic_one_finger: the click is derived from the summed
  pressure of all fingers, so two fingers resting to scroll can click. Each
  finger beyond the first can raise every threshold, or only one finger may
  start a click.
- haptic_deep_keycode can change while the driver runs. The Force Click input
  device always exists and offers F13 to F19; the key that went down is the
  one let go.
- haptic_release_strength: a strength of its own for the release waveform.
- A change of haptic_press starts the mode worker at once, instead of waiting
  for the next touch, and clears the count of earlier refusals. Each refusal
  is logged.

